From 6a722e4cbd4c9a5643f146db43171fc16089e920 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vgatherps <vgatherps@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:52:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] unbuffered: return received app data in place

`ReadTraffic::next_record` copied every application data record into a
fresh `Vec` (`take_received_plaintext` -> `into_vec`) and lent that out,
although the record had already been decrypted in place inside the
caller's `incoming_tls` buffer. This resolves the TODO on `next_record`
("requires in-place decryption"): unbuffered connections no longer copy
or allocate per received record.

- `AppDataRecord::payload` is now `&'i mut [u8]`, a slice of
  `incoming_tls` holding the decrypted plaintext. It borrows the buffer,
  so the caller cannot discard or reuse it while the payload is alive.
- The record's bytes are no longer part of `UnbufferedStatus::discard`;
  they are reported in `AppDataRecord::discard`, as that field documents.
  The unbuffered fuzzer now adds it.
- A `ReadTraffic` dropped without calling `next_record` still presents
  the same record on the next `process_tls_records` call; the connection
  remembers where its plaintext lies and does not decrypt it again.
- Buffered connections are unchanged.
